  m_text: '<size=135%><color=#382C30><b>Privacy Policy</b></color></size>

    Last
    updated: 12 October 2026


    <size=108%><b>1. Introduction</b></size>

    GlowUp
    ("we", "our", or "us") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your
    personal data. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and
    safeguard your information when you use our mobile application. Please read this
    privacy policy carefully. If you do not agree with the terms of this privacy
    policy, please do not access the application.


    <size=108%><b>2. Information
    We Collect</b></size>

    We collect information that you voluntarily provide
    to us when registering for an account and while using the application. This includes:


    <indent=4%>-
    Personal Identifiers: your first name, middle name, last name, date of birth,
    age, and email address.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- Profile and Preference Data:
    your skin type, skin tone, skin conditions, and known cosmetic allergens and
    sensitivities. This information is used exclusively to tailor the app''s safety
    analyses and product recommendations to your personal profile.</indent>

    <indent=4%>-
    Scan Data: the ingredient text read from product labels, the results of each
    analysis, the products you save to your Recent Scans, and any names you give
    them.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- Suggestions: skin conditions, allergens, or
    ingredients you add that are not yet in our lists, so that we can review them
    and improve the database.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- Technical Data: our cloud
    provider may process basic technical information, such as your IP address and
    device identifiers, in order to deliver and secure the service.</indent>


    <size=108%><b>3.
    How We Use Your Information</b></size>

    Having accurate information permits
    us to provide you with a smooth, efficient, and customized experience. Specifically,
    we use information collected via GlowUp to:


    <indent=4%>- Create and secure
    your user account using Google Firebase Authentication.</indent>

    <indent=4%>-
    Confirm that the email address is yours. When you sign up with an email and password,
    your account is created as soon as the first sign-up page is filled in, and Google
    Firebase Authentication sends a message with a link to that address. The sign-up
    goes on once you have tapped the link. If you leave the sign-up before finishing
    it, that unfinished account is removed again.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- Make
    sure the email address you sign up with can really receive email. For an address
    that is not from a well-known provider, the app asks a public internet directory
    (DNS, run by Google or Cloudflare) whether the part after the @ (for example
    "school.edu.ph") has a mail server. Only that part is sent, never your name or
    the whole address. Temporary ("throw-away") email addresses cannot be used to
    sign up.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- Store and retrieve your profile preferences
    securely using Google Cloud Firestore.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- Personalize
    cosmetic ingredient safety assessments and filter recommendations based on your
    registered skin type, skin conditions, age, and allergies.</indent>

    <indent=4%>-
    Keep your scan history available across sessions and, when you are online, across
    your devices.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- Count how often a brand is scanned,
    without attaching your name to that count, so that we can prioritise which products
    to add to the database.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- Communicate with you regarding
    account updates, security alerts, and support messages.</indent>


    <size=108%><b>4.
    Camera, Scans, and AR Try-On</b></size>

    GlowUp asks for permission to use
    your camera for three features: scanning a product and its ingredient list, previewing
    shades on your face with AR Try-On, and (only if you switch it on in Settings)
    finger signs, which change screen when you hold 1 to 5 fingers up to the selfie
    camera.


    <indent=4%>- The text on a product is read on your device. We do
    not record or store the live camera feed, and we keep no photos.</indent>

    <indent=4%>-
    For a scan, only the text that was read, the product''s name and the result are
    kept and analysed. When you are online and the app cannot name the product by
    itself, a few still pictures of the PRODUCT you are holding (its front, back
    or bottom; four at most, once per scan) may be sent to our AI service provider
    so that the product can be recognised (see section 5). Those pictures are not
    saved by us.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- So that the app knows a product again
    the next time you scan it, it keeps what its pack looks like as a set of numbers
    (not a picture; the picture cannot be rebuilt from them), together with any other
    name you typed for the product. These stay on your device only and are removed
    when you clear the app''s data or uninstall the app.</indent>

    <indent=4%>-
    For AR Try-On, the picture of your face is used only while the preview is on
    screen. It is not saved and it is never sent to us or to anyone else.</indent>

    <indent=4%>-
    For finger signs, the selfie camera''s picture is looked at on your device only,
    to count the fingers of the hand you hold up. It is not saved and it is never
    sent to us or to anyone else. Finger signs are off until you switch them on,
    and your phone shows its "camera in use" sign while they are on.</indent>


    You
    can withdraw camera permission at any time in your device settings. The scanning
    and try-on features will stop working until permission is given again, but you
    can still type ingredients in by hand.


    <size=108%><b>5. AI-Assisted Analysis</b></size>

    Part
    of each analysis is produced automatically. When you are online, the following
    may be sent to our AI service provider: up to four still pictures of the product,
    the text read from it, the product''s name, and ingredient names. This is used
    to recognise the product, to find its published ingredient list, and to describe
    ingredients that are not yet in our database. The product''s name may also be
    sent to the FDA Philippines verification site to check whether the product is
    registered. When the camera read the product''s barcode, that barcode (and nothing
    else) may be sent to Open Beauty Facts, a public list of cosmetics, to compare
    its ingredient list with the one the app has.


    Your profile is never sent
    to the AI service. Your name, email address, password, age, skin type, skin tone,
    skin conditions, and allergens stay out of every such request: the comparison
    between a product and your profile is made on your device.


    Automated results
    can be incomplete or wrong. Please read section 4 of the Terms and Conditions
    below.


    <size=108%><b>6. Data Security and Third-Party Services</b></size>

    We
    implement industry-standard security measures, including encrypted transit layers
    (HTTPS) and salted password hashing, to protect your personal information. Your
    password is never stored in readable form. We utilize Google Firebase as our
    primary cloud backend infrastructure. Google Firebase adheres to rigorous security
    standards. We do not sell, trade, or otherwise transfer your personally identifiable
    information to outside parties.


    No method of transmission or storage is
    completely secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security, and you use the application
    with that understanding.


    <size=108%><b>7. Offline Use</b></size>

    To
    let GlowUp work without an internet connection, a copy of your profile, your
    scan history, and the ingredient database is kept on your device. Changes you
    make offline are sent to the cloud the next time you are online. If you share
    your device with other people, sign out when you are finished.


    The email
    addresses that have signed in with a password on this device are also kept on
    the device, so that the log-in page can offer them under the email field. You
    can take an address off that list there at any time, and it is removed when you
    delete your account or clear the app''s data in your phone''s settings. Only
    the address is kept: passwords are never shown, offered, or stored in readable
    form. The app shows this list of its own instead of your phone''s saved accounts.


    <size=108%><b>8.
    Data Retention and Account Deletion</b></size>

    We retain your personal data
    only for as long as your account is active or as needed to provide you with app
    services. You have the right to request the deletion of your account and all
    associated data at any time by contacting our support team.


    <size=108%><b>9.
    Children''s Privacy</b></size>

    GlowUp is not intended for children under
    13 years of age, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from them. If
    you believe a child under 13 has created an account, please contact us so that
    we can remove it.


    <size=108%><b>10. Your Rights and Choices</b></size>

    Depending
    on where you live, you may have the right to see the personal data we hold about
    you, to correct it, to ask for it to be deleted, and to withdraw your consent.
    You can update your profile in the app at any time, and you can contact us for
    any other request.


    <size=108%><b>11. Changes to This Policy</b></size>

    We
    may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will change
    the "Last updated" date at the top and, where the change is significant, tell
    you inside the app.


    <size=108%><b>12. Contact Us</b></size>

    If you
    have questions about this Privacy Policy, contact our support team at: [add your
    support email here]



    <size=135%><color=#382C30><b>Terms and Conditions</b></color></size>


    <size=108%><b>1.
    Acceptance of Terms</b></size>

    By downloading, installing, or creating an
    account on GlowUp, you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions. If you
    disagree with any part of these terms, you must discontinue use of the application
    immediately.


    <size=108%><b>2. Eligibility</b></size>

    You must be at
    least 13 years old to use GlowUp. If you are under 18, you confirm that a parent
    or guardian has read and agreed to these terms on your behalf.


    <size=108%><b>3.
    Medical and Dermatological Disclaimer</b></size>

    <indent=4%>- Not a Medical
    Device: GlowUp is designed strictly as a cosmetic safety and ingredient-analysis
    tool. It is not a medical device, clinical diagnostic tool, or a substitute for
    professional dermatological advice, diagnosis, or treatment.</indent>

    <indent=4%>-
    Consult a Professional: always seek the advice of a licensed dermatologist or
    qualified healthcare provider with any questions you may have regarding a medical
    skin condition, severe dermatitis, or acute allergic reactions. Never disregard
    professional medical advice or delay in seeking it because of information provided
    by GlowUp.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- Patch Testing: cosmetic formulations react
    differently across individuals. Users are strongly advised to perform a patch
    test on a small area of skin before applying any new skincare product, regardless
    of the app''s safety result or ingredient analysis.</indent>


    <size=108%><b>4.
    Ingredient Analysis and AI Results</b></size>

    The results shown by GlowUp
    are generated automatically from the text read off a product label, from our
    ingredient database, and from an AI service. They are provided for general information
    only.


    <indent=4%>- The camera can misread a label, and manufacturers change
    their formulas. Always check the ingredient list printed on the product you actually
    hold.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- An ingredient that is not yet in our database
    is not part of the result. A result of "safe" means that nothing in our records
    conflicts with your profile. It is not a guarantee that you will not react to
    the product.</indent>

    <indent=4%>- A result of "caution" or "harmful" is
    a prompt to look more closely or to ask a professional. It is not a diagnosis.</indent>


    <size=108%><b>5.
    AR Try-On</b></size>

    AR Try-On shows a simulated preview. Colours and finish
    depend on your screen, your camera, and the lighting around you, and the real
    product may look different on your skin. The preview is not a promise of how
    a product will look or perform.


    <size=108%><b>6. Product Information and
    Recommendations</b></size>

    Product, brand, and ingredient information is
    supplied by our team and by third parties and may be incomplete or out of date.
    A recommendation in the app is not an endorsement, and we do not guarantee that
    a recommended product is available where you live.


    <size=108%><b>7. User
    Accounts and Responsibilities</b></size>

    <indent=4%>- You are responsible
    for maintaining the confidentiality of your login credentials and password.</indent>

    <indent=4%>-
    You agree to provide accurate, current, and complete information during the onboarding
    and registration process and to keep your profile updated.</indent>

    <indent=4%>-
    You agree not to use the app for any unlawful purpose or in any way that could
    damage, disable, or impair the application''s infrastructure.</indent>


    <size=108%><b>8.
    Acceptable Use</b></size>

    You agree not to copy or extract the database
    in bulk, attempt to bypass the security of the application, use the application
    to harass or harm another person, or submit content that is unlawful, misleading,
    or that you do not have the right to share.


    <size=108%><b>9. Your Suggestions</b></size>

    When
    you suggest a skin condition, allergen, ingredient, or product, you allow us
    to review it, edit it, and add it to the database so that other users can benefit
    from it. Do not include personal or confidential information in a suggestion.


    <size=108%><b>10.
    Intellectual Property Rights</b></size>

    The GlowUp name, logo, source code,
    design elements, and underlying software are the intellectual property of the
    developers. You may not copy, modify, distribute, or reverse-engineer any portion
    of this application without express written permission.


    <size=108%><b>11.
    Third-Party Services</b></size>

    GlowUp relies on services operated by other
    companies, including Google Firebase and, if you choose to use them, sign-in
    services such as Google or Facebook. Your use of those services is also subject
    to their own terms and privacy policies.


    <size=108%><b>12. Suspension and
    Termination</b></size>

    You may stop using GlowUp at any time. We may suspend
    or close an account that breaks these terms or that puts the service or other
    users at risk.


    <size=108%><b>13. Limitation of Liability</b></size>

    To
